WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:18.392
On last day of camp, the air buzzed with excitement.

2
00:00:19.312 --> 00:00:23.755
Iris dropped off her lunch and hurried to join Grace and the other girls at the courts.

3
00:00:27.558 --> 00:00:29.680
She was ready to play tennis!

4
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.362
Until something strange caught her attention.

5
00:00:33.962 --> 00:00:36.104
Javier was striding toward Jae.

6
00:00:38.726 --> 00:00:44.350
He muttered something to Jae and then beckoned him over to a secluded spot near a pine tree.

7
00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.291
"What's going on?"

8
00:00:46.951 --> 00:00:47.572
Iris thought.

9
00:00:48.292 --> 00:00:49.973
She moved closer to the boys.

10
00:00:49.993 --> 00:00:59.260
"I know what you tried with my sister, and I don't like it," Javier snapped, scowling.

11
00:01:00.276 --> 00:01:02.238
"Wha-what are you talking about?"

12
00:01:02.778 --> 00:01:03.579
Jae stammered.

13
00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.904
"You were trying to convince her to join the older kids' group so you could laugh at her,"

14
00:01:10.545 --> 00:01:11.445
Javier said.

15
00:01:11.465 --> 00:01:14.388
"I heard you and Zoe talking about it."

16
00:01:15.889 --> 00:01:17.390
Iris' face flamed.

17
00:01:17.971 --> 00:01:21.213
That was why Jae had suggested they could be doubles partners?

18
00:01:21.233 --> 00:01:25.096
"Dude, I was just goofing around."

19
00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:27.498
Jae let out a feeble laugh.

20
00:01:27.518 --> 00:01:30.733
"Besides, it was Zoe's idea.

21
00:01:31.493 --> 00:01:36.616
Zoe thinks your sister likes me, so she told me to say that to Iris to see what

22
00:01:36.656 --> 00:01:37.176
would happen."

23
00:01:38.757 --> 00:01:40.318
Javier raised his voice.

24
00:01:40.338 --> 00:01:42.940
"Leave Iris alone.

25
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:43.920
Got it?"

26
00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.201
"Yeah, man, whatever."

27
00:01:49.263 --> 00:01:53.866
They broke apart, and Iris ducked behind a tree as the boys walked by.

28
00:01:55.426 --> 00:01:59.212
Javier had been trying to protect her from Jae!

29
00:01:59.232 --> 00:02:01.234
That helped Iris to feel a little better.

30
00:02:01.774 --> 00:02:04.216
But still Jae didn't like her.

31
00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:10.080
He'd only been making fun of her—and she had almost fallen for it!

32
00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.383
"Focus," a voice inside Iris commanded.

33
00:02:15.103 --> 00:02:18.385
She'd played enough soccer games to know how to compete mentally.

34
00:02:18.405 --> 00:02:22.668
"Stop thinking about Jae, and think about your game."

35
00:02:23.489 --> 00:02:29.777
Ally had basically told Iris the same thing: when you're playing tennis, you have to think about tennis.

36
00:02:31.057 --> 00:02:34.918
Iris inhaled deeply and raced over to join her group.

37
00:02:38.679 --> 00:02:39.419
"Hi, everyone!"

38
00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.080
Ally was beaming.

39
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.521
"It's time to announce final partners and matchups."

40
00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:49.022
Everyone cheered, including Iris.

41
00:02:49.042 --> 00:02:55.144
"We'll start with Anna and Kaylee against Alex and Oliver," Ally went on.

42
00:02:56.268 --> 00:03:04.234
"And next Risa and Natalie against Akira and Aiden, and the final matchup will be Iris and Grace

43
00:03:04.695 --> 00:03:06.436
against Javier and Ben.

44
00:03:07.337 --> 00:03:09.519
Anyway, we'll play after lunch.

45
00:03:10.219 --> 00:03:13.542
For now, we get to watch the older kids play."

46
00:03:14.763 --> 00:03:22.849
During the morning's matches, Iris paid close attention, carefully noting the older kids' skills—the way they returned the

47
00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:25.792
ball and looked for opportunities to score points.

48
00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:30.741
But she could barely watch when Jae played doubles with Zoe.

49
00:03:31.481 --> 00:03:36.123
When they won, they grinned and high-fived as if they'd just won Wimbledon.

50
00:03:37.443 --> 00:03:40.064
How could she have once thought that Jae was nice?

51
00:03:41.224 --> 00:03:46.025
Grace did some last-minute coaching of Iris, Anna, and Risa during lunch.

52
00:03:47.065 --> 00:03:52.227
"Remember, the boys will try to hit to you three newbies as often as possible.

53
00:03:53.007 --> 00:03:54.127
But you guys are ready."

54
00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:55.928
"Let's go!"

55
00:03:56.784 --> 00:03:57.404
Ally called.

56
00:03:59.065 --> 00:04:03.267
Julie, the camp director, signaled the first players into position.

57
00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:11.491
Anna and Kaylee won their match against Alex and Oliver, but Akira and Aiden beat Risa and Natalie.

58
00:04:12.711 --> 00:04:17.073
It was up to Iris and Grace to put the final win in the girls' column.

59
00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:20.334
Iris looked across the net at her brother.

60
00:04:21.675 --> 00:04:28.214
She still wanted to do her best, but her strong desire to beat Javier had disappeared.

61
00:04:29.255 --> 00:04:30.496
Ben served the ball.

62
00:04:32.377 --> 00:04:33.998
It rocketed right at Iris.

63
00:04:34.738 --> 00:04:40.381
Standing with her feet hip-width apart, she kept her eyes on the ball and batted it right back.

64
00:04:42.242 --> 00:04:45.864
Before either boy reached the ball, it landed with a thud.

65
00:04:45.884 --> 00:04:49.967
"Love–fifteen!" Julie called.

66
00:04:49.987 --> 00:04:54.297
"Whoa!" Iris' mouth dropped open.

67
00:04:55.058 --> 00:04:56.839
She had scored the first point!

68
00:04:57.519 --> 00:05:04.404
Along the sideline, people fist-bumped, reminding Iris that fans weren't supposed to cheer loudly like in soccer.

69
00:05:05.245 --> 00:05:07.166
She wondered if Jae was watching her.

70
00:05:07.766 --> 00:05:12.390
But before she could find him in the crowd, Ben served straight to her again.

71
00:05:15.131 --> 00:05:18.914
She swung but only managed to tip the ball with her racket.

72
00:05:19.574 --> 00:05:21.596
The ball crashed down to her feet.

73
00:05:24.376 --> 00:05:25.756
"Fifteen all!"

74
00:05:26.597 --> 00:05:27.997
The score was tied.

75
00:05:30.298 --> 00:05:36.119
The games, and then the sets, went on, with the lead flipping back and forth between the girls'

76
00:05:36.179 --> 00:05:37.119
and boys' teams.

77
00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:44.261
One point for Iris' team, and then one for Javier's, until they were on the seventh game of

78
00:05:44.301 --> 00:05:45.282
the third set.

79
00:05:47.142 --> 00:05:49.223
Sweat dripped down Iris' neck.

80
00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:54.164
It was down to the last point, and it was Javier's turn to serve.

81
00:05:54.964 --> 00:05:57.987
Javier tossed the ball into the air and swung.

82
00:05:59.628 --> 00:06:02.450
The ball landed closer to Iris than to Grace.

83
00:06:03.371 --> 00:06:07.254
Iris knew she could win the game with one well-executed fake.

84
00:06:08.215 --> 00:06:09.916
Her eyes flicked toward Javier.

85
00:06:10.577 --> 00:06:11.417
He was her brother.

86
00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.660
Her annoying sloth of a brother.

87
00:06:15.521 --> 00:06:19.584
The same brother who had gotten furious at Jae for being mean to her.

88
00:06:19.604 --> 00:06:24.088
For a millisecond she was tempted to let him win.

89
00:06:24.908 --> 00:06:31.990
But she was a competitive athlete and a good teammate, so instead Iris dove for the ball.

90
00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:35.031
She twisted her body for the fake.

91
00:06:38.252 --> 00:06:42.333
The ball sailed over the net toward Javier, who missed it.

92
00:06:46.574 --> 00:06:47.614
set, match!"

93
00:06:48.355 --> 00:06:48.975
Ally called.

94
00:06:50.475 --> 00:06:53.076
Iris and Grace raised their rackets in victory.

95
00:06:54.336 --> 00:06:56.357
Disappointment filled Ben's face.

96
00:06:57.018 --> 00:06:58.058
Javier's too.

97
00:06:58.078 --> 00:07:03.081
"Good game, girls," the boys said, stepping toward the net to shake hands.

98
00:07:04.122 --> 00:07:05.422
Iris approached her brother.

99
00:07:05.442 --> 00:07:09.185
"I heard what you said, Javier."

100
00:07:09.205 --> 00:07:10.846
"What are you talking about?"

101
00:07:10.866 --> 00:07:12.406
"To Jae."

102
00:07:13.047 --> 00:07:14.608
Iris looked her brother in the eye.

103
00:07:14.628 --> 00:07:15.608
"Thank you."

104
00:07:15.628 --> 00:07:17.890
"Oh, that."

105
00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.430
Javier shrugged.

106
00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:20.571
"You're welcome.

107
00:07:21.131 --> 00:07:21.892
He's a jerk."

108
00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.361
Iris nodded as she shook her brother's hand.

109
00:07:26.882 --> 00:07:29.243
"We completely agree on that, bro!"

110
00:07:31.585 --> 00:07:32.685
"How did it go today?"

111
00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:34.506
Mama called from the kitchen.

112
00:07:35.267 --> 00:07:39.529
She'd come home from work a bit early and was frying something on the stovetop.

113
00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.751
Iris followed Javier down the hall.

114
00:07:42.771 --> 00:07:47.593
"Steak!" he announced.

115
00:07:49.674 --> 00:07:52.456
Iris couldn't remember the last time they'd had steak.

116
00:07:53.312 --> 00:07:54.473
Her mouth watered.

117
00:07:55.613 --> 00:07:59.976
Javier smiled at Mama, and Mama smiled back at both of them.

118
00:08:00.676 --> 00:08:04.458
Then she set the steak on a cutting board and waved at the table.

119
00:08:04.478 --> 00:08:09.381
"Come and sit, and tell me all about the last day of camp."

120
00:08:09.401 --> 00:08:13.083
"Iris won the final match," Javier said.

121
00:08:13.103 --> 00:08:18.266
"But Javier's team almost beat us," Iris said quickly.

122
00:08:18.286 --> 00:08:22.148
"It was a close game, and he really improved a lot.

123
00:08:22.796 --> 00:08:23.977
We both did, in fact."

124
00:08:25.658 --> 00:08:29.641
"Sounds like it was a good experience for both of you then," Mama said.

125
00:08:30.442 --> 00:08:31.082
They nodded.

126
00:08:31.102 --> 00:08:33.744
"Good," Mama said.

127
00:08:33.764 --> 00:08:36.487
"Because summer is not over yet.

128
00:08:37.167 --> 00:08:39.709
And I signed you up for another camp."

129
00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:43.792
"Huh?" Iris looked at Mama in surprise.

130
00:08:43.812 --> 00:08:48.636
"It was the only camp that still had openings," Mama went on.

131
00:08:49.928 --> 00:08:53.031
"And you'll be happy to know it's not tennis camp."

132
00:08:53.051 --> 00:08:54.712
"What is it?"

133
00:08:55.373 --> 00:08:56.354
Javier sighed.

134
00:08:58.055 --> 00:08:59.076
Mama smiled.

135
00:09:00.077 --> 00:09:01.057
"Math camp."

136
00:09:01.938 --> 00:09:02.839
Math camp?

137
00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:07.203
Iris and Javier looked at each other and burst out laughing.

138
00:09:09.525 --> 00:09:15.470
One thing was sure: if they'd survived tennis camp, they could survive anything.

139
00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:17.811
Even math camp.
